# Git workflow (two people, two Cursors)

Work lands on a personal branch. `main` stays green and is updated only by an explicit merge after the full check passes.

## Before the first edit

1. `git fetch origin`
2. `git checkout main && git pull`
3. Create a new branch: `<name>/<short-slice>` (examples: `matteo/grid-move`, `d20/companion-voice`).
4. Never commit on `main`. Never reuse or push to the other person's branch.

One branch, one slice. If the task changes, open another branch.

## Stay in your tree

Say which directories you will touch, then stay there. `packages/protocol`, `packages/rules`, `package.json`, and `package-lock.json` are shared: edit them only when the task requires it, and say so before changing them.

## Before merging into main

Do this on the feature branch, after it contains the latest `origin/main`:

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
npm run typecheck && NARRATION=off npm test && npm run build
```

If `firetv/` changed, also run `./gradlew --no-daemon lintRelease assembleRelease` from `firetv/`.

Merge only when every command exits 0 and the user explicitly asks to merge. A failing check is fixed on the branch. Do not merge to "fix it on main".
